PHASE 4 — POSTGRESQL VIA DOCKER
Postgres runs in Docker. Clean, isolated, easy to backup and restore.

# Create data directory on host for persistence

mkdir -p /opt/orbit/postgres/data

# Create the postgres container

docker run -d \

    --name orbit-postgres \

    --restart unless-stopped \

    -e POSTGRES_USER=orbit \

    -e POSTGRES_PASSWORD=CHANGE_THIS_PASSWORD \

    -e POSTGRES_DB=orbit \

    -v /opt/orbit/postgres/data:/var/lib/postgresql/data \

    -p 127.0.0.1:5432:5432 \

    postgres:16-alpine

# Verify

docker ps | grep orbit-postgres

docker exec -it orbit-postgres psql -U orbit -c "\l"

Postgres is bound to 127.0.0.1 only — not accessible from outside the server.
