NOTES FOR CURSOR
Teardown first, no exceptions. Run Phase 1 discovery, paste output, then run teardown. Don't skip to install phases.

Postgres runs in Docker, everything else is systemd. OpenD and the bot cannot run in Docker — OpenD needs persistent socket connections and file system access that Docker complicates.

Python 3.11 specifically. moomoo-api recommends 3.11. Ubuntu 24 ships 3.12 — install 3.11 via deadsnakes PPA.

--workers 1 on uvicorn. Non-negotiable. Bot asyncio tasks live in-process. Multiple workers breaks everything.

frontend/dist is committed to Git. This is intentional. Northstar pulls and serves the pre-built files via Caddy. No Node.js runtime needed on the server.

OpenD binaries are NOT committed to Git. They go in /opt/orbit/opend/{user}/ directly. Download from moomoo and place manually. .gitignore excludes them.

Secrets never in Git. .env, google_credentials.json, OpenD.xml passwords — all in .gitignore. Copy them to the server manually or via scp.

EAS builds run in the cloud. You don't need Xcode on the Mac Mini for production builds. EAS handles it. You DO need Xcode installed for local development/simulator builds.

Apple credentials for EAS. You need an Apple Developer account ($99/year). EAS will prompt for credentials on first build and store them securely.

Bundle ID is final. com.ncs.orbitfabio — once submitted to App Store Connect this cannot change.

